.TH MEET 1 "2026" "meet @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
meet \- open a saved meeting link by name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B meet
[\fINAME\fR]
.br
.B meet
\fB\-\-add\fR \fINAME\fR \fIURL\fR
.br
.B meet
\fB\-\-delete\fR \fINAME\fR
.br
.B meet
\fB\-\-list\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B meet
keeps a short list of meeting URLs under names you choose, so a recurring
call is
.B meet standup
instead of a bookmark hunt.
.PP
With no arguments it offers an interactive picker:
.BR fzf (1)
if it is installed, otherwise a plain numbered menu. With a name it opens
that meeting through
.BR xdg\-open (1).
.PP
Nothing about it is Google\-specific \(em any URL works.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-add " " \fINAME\fR " " \fIURL\fR
Save a meeting. The name may not contain spaces, and the URL must start with
\fBhttp://\fR or \fBhttps://\fR. Adding a name that already exists is refused
rather than silently duplicated.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delete " " \fINAME\fR
Forget a saved meeting.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List saved meetings, name and URL.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print " " \fINAME\fR
Print the URL to standard output instead of opening it.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Read and write this links file instead of the default.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be opened without opening it.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.meet/links
Used when it already exists, so upgrading does not lose your list.
.TP
.B ~/.config/meet/links
Used otherwise. One \fBNAME URL\fR pair per line.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEET_LINKS
Overrides the links file, like
.BR \-\-file .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No such meeting, or nothing saved yet.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage, or
.B xdg\-open
is missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
meet \-\-add standup https://meet.google.com/abc\-defg\-hij
meet standup
meet \-\-list
meet \-\-delete standup
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg\-open (1),
.BR fzf (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @MAINTAINER@.
